# Local env files must never be uploaded to a Vercel build.
#
# Being gitignored is NOT enough: the Vercel CLI uploads them anyway, and Vite
# then inlines their values into the production bundle for any variable that is
# not also set in the Vercel project's own env settings (a real env var wins
# over a .env file; an absent one does not).
#
# This bit for real on 2026-08-07 (§6.7): VITE_API_BASE_URL was safe because
# Vercel had its own value, but VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY did not exist there, so
# the LOCAL dev VAPID key was shipped to production. Push subscriptions are
# cryptographically bound to the key that created them, so production would
# have handed out subscriptions its own backend could never push to — rejected
# with a 403 and swallowed per-subscription, i.e. failing completely silently
# behind a toggle that looked like it worked.
.env
.env.*
